  "notes": "Cash basis county, governmental funds only. beginning_cash = fund balances beginning of year (p4, total governmental funds 3,836,368); ending_cash = total assets / fund balances 3,264,079 (p1, p3, p4). Taxes 954,893 split into property 894,074 and motor vehicle 60,819 using the statement of activities general receipts (p2); they add to the printed line. Local 296,521 split into interest 169,247, charges for services 116,165 and miscellaneous 11,109 using the statement of activities (p2); they add to the printed line. Transfers in/out 320,586 each are inter-fund within governmental funds (p4); sale of surplus 22,095 is printed under other financing sources (Road Fund). Identity: 3,836,368 + 2,200,273 - 2,794,657 + 320,586 - 320,586 + 22,095 = 3,264,079. Detail: General Fund recorded from the budgetary comparison schedule (p8; departments, no object breakdown) rather than the General Fund combining statement (p5, function-level) to avoid double counting; the p5 Inheritance Tax fund (part of the combined General Fund on the statements) is recorded separately. Schedule p8 General Fund budget transfers (in 45,893, out 254,479) are gross and differ from p5 columns (net -208,586 both). General government 'Miscellaneous' department 214,911 plus other departments sums to 1,197,590, which includes capital outlay of the General fund (32,248) and culture/recreation 9,000, so department totals differ from the statement function split. Road Fund actual local receipts on p9 (28,646) include 22,095 sale of surplus that p4 presents as other financing. Emergency Road and Road single-line disbursements recorded as not itemized. No business-type funds, no proprietary statement. Read pages 1-11 of 11."
